.TH CCODE-TUI 1 "September 2026" "ccode v0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccode-tui \- terminal AI coding assistant (split TUI frontend)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccode-tui
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NOTE (September 2026, temporary):
.B ccode-tui
is paused and no longer built; only
.BR ccode-cli (1)
is shipped. This page is kept for reference.
.PP
.B ccode-tui
is the split terminal frontend: it renders the conversation in an ANSI
terminal, streams backend output as it arrives, and shows tool
permission prompts, while the agent itself runs in a separate
.BR ccode-cli (1)
backend process driven over the JSON Lines protocol on stdin/stdout.
It is always interactive; no
.B \-i
or prompt flag is required.
.PP
The backend is located in this order:
.BR \-\-backend ,
.BR CCODE_BACKEND ,
a
.B ccode-cli
next to the
.B ccode-tui
executable, and finally
.B ccode-cli
via
.BR PATH .
If the backend cannot be started,
.B ccode-tui
reports it: build
.B ccode-cli
alongside it, or set
.BR CCODE_BACKEND .
.SH OPTIONS
Options mirror
.BR ccode-cli (1)
(agent, model, tools, sessions); the frontend-relevant ones are:
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " PATH"
Backend executable to drive (see DESCRIPTION for the lookup order).
.TP
.B \-\-write
Enable read and write tools (approved interactively in the TUI).
.TP
.B \-\-read-only
Read-only tools (read_file, glob, grep, git_*). This is the default mode.
.TP
.B \-\-default
Fast start preset: read/write tools plus thinking at
.BR high " effort."
Never enables
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
.TP
.B \-\-thinking
Send the
.B "thinking"
field
.RB ( type:
.BR enabled ).
On by default; disable with
.BR CCODE_THINKING=0 .
.TP
.B \-\-reasoning
Send the reasoning_effort field (default effort:
.BR high ).
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-effort " LEVEL"
Reasoning effort:
.BR low ", " medium ", " high ", " xhigh
or
.BR max .
.TP
.BI \-\-thinking-effort " LEVEL"
Alias for
.BR \-\-reasoning-effort .
.TP
.B \-\-no-markdown
Disable markdown rendering (raw output).
.TP
.BI \-\-session-dir " DIR"
Session storage directory (defaults to
.BR CCODE_SESSION_DIR ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Submit the input line.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Cancel the in-flight request (press twice to quit).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-D / Ctrl\-Q
Quit the TUI.
.PP
Additional editing keys follow common readline conventions (arrows,
home/end, backspace, etc.).
.PP
Slash commands are executed by the backend; see
.BR ccode-cli (1)
for the list. Unlike the single-binary
.BR ccode (1)
TUI, there is no in-process
.B /compact
restriction here: if the backend supports it, it works.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR ccode-cli (1)
for the full list. Relevant to the frontend:
.TP
.B CCODE_BACKEND
Backend executable path (overrides the same-directory default).
.TP
.B CCODE_WORKSPACE
Workspace directory (defaults to the current directory).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ccode/sessions/
Conversation session files (JSON).
